[center][size=6][b][color=#b48cff]S3MAPHORE[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Your music. Your rules.[/i][/size]

[b][i]Brought to You by DreamWeave-MP[/i][/b][/center]

[center][size=4][b]Modern, contextual music management for OpenMW.[/b][/size]

No compromises. No bullshit. Your music responds to the world around you.[/center]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]REQUIREMENTS[/color][/center]
[/heading]

[list]
[*][b]OpenMW 0.51 or newer[/b] — [url=https://openmw.org/downloads]Download OpenMW[/url][/*]
[*][b]H3lp Yours3lf[/b] — [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/56417]Download H3lp Yours3lf[/url][/*]
[/list]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]INSTALLATION — START HERE[/color][/center]
[/heading]

[center][size=5][b][color=#ffcc66]Enable 00 Core and S3maphore.esp.[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Everything else in the S3maphore archive is optional.[/b][/center]

[size=4][b]Using an OpenMW mod manager[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]1.[/b] Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/56417]H3lp Yours3lf[/url].[/*]
[*][b]2.[/b] Install S3maphore.[/*]
[*][b]3.[/b] Enable the [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] data directory.[/*]
[*][b]4.[/b] Enable [font=Courier New]S3maphore.esp[/font] in OpenMW's content list.[/*]
[*][b]5.[/b] Enable only optional modules matching music or content you use.[/*]
[*][b]6.[/b] Launch the game. Vanilla Explore and Battle music should work immediately.[/*]
[/list]

[color=#ffcc66][b]Do not enable every module blindly.[/b][/color] Most optional modules define playlists for music supplied by another mod. If S3maphore finds no matching tracks, the playlist stays inactive.

[size=4][b]Manual OpenMW installation[/b][/size]

S3maphore is packaged as several OpenMW data directories. Do [b]not[/b] flatten them into Morrowind's [font=Courier New]Data Files[/font] directory.

Keep them separate and add only the directories you want to [font=Courier New]openmw.cfg[/font].

For example:

[code]data="/path/to/S3maphore/00 Core"
data="/path/to/S3maphore/03 Muse Expansion Playlists"[/code]

Add [font=Courier New]S3maphore.esp[/font] from [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] to your OpenMW content list.

[color=#d4d4d8][b]Important:[/b] module numbers are labels, not load-order numbers. They do not need to be enabled in numerical order.[/color]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]WHAT S3MAPHORE DOES[/color][/center]
[/heading]

S3maphore replaces OpenMW's built-in music handling with contextual playlists.

Music can react to location, region, cell, faction, enemy, weather, time, tileset, magic effects, or damn near anything else OpenMW exposes to Lua.

The mental model is simple:

[list]
[*][b]Playlist[/b] — a collection of tracks with rules for when it may play.[/*]
[*][b]Priority[/b] — decides which valid playlist wins.[/*]
[*][b]Playdeck[/b] — every playlist S3maphore discovers in your OpenMW installation.[/*]
[/list]

When the game state changes, S3maphore checks the playdeck and [b]deals[/b] the highest-priority valid playlist.

Battle music is not magic. It is just a playlist with a combat rule and a high priority.

OpenMW dehardcoded its music system during the 0.49 development cycle, but its public playlist API was removed before release. S3maphore restores that missing layer and builds a complete playlist system on top of it.

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]MODULES[/color][/center]
[/heading]

Each S3maphore module is an OpenMW data directory containing playlist definitions, music, or both.

[size=4][b]Required[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] — the S3maphore engine plus vanilla [font=Courier New]Music/Explore[/font] and [font=Courier New]Music/Battle[/font] playlists. It does not include replacement music.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Major playlist modules[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]01 Tamriel Rebuilt Playlists[/font] — support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/47254]Tamriel Rebuilt - Original Soundtrack[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]02 Project Cyrodiil Playlists[/font] — support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/55779]Project Cyrodiil Music - Anvil and Sutch[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]03 Muse Expansion Playlists[/font] — compatibility playlists for MUSE-style music packs, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51734]Morrow Winds[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51769]CaptainCreepy Music Pack[/url], and related music mods.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Extended modules[/b][/size]

These are optional and may require a separate music or content mod.

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]04 Vindsvept Solstheim[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53597]Vindsvept Solstheim for Dynamic Music[/url].[/*]
