[/list]

The optional [font=Courier New]01 TAVERNS[/font] module is supported by [font=Courier New]10 Inns and Taverns[/font].

The optional [font=Courier New]02 VAMPIRE COMBAT[/font] module is supported through [font=Courier New]Muse Vampire.lua[/font] using [font=Courier New]Music/MS/combat/Vampire[/font].[/spoiler]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]USAGE[/color][/center]
[/heading]

[size=4][b]Adding your own music[/b][/size]

Most S3maphore playlists read supported tracks from a folder.

The empty [font=Courier New]Music[/font] folders included with playlist modules are intentional drop zones. You do not need to edit Lua.

For example, this track becomes available to the Hlaalu playlist:

[code]03 Muse Expansion Playlists/Music/ms/cell/hlaalu/my-hlaalu-track.mp3[/code]

You can provide the same [font=Courier New]Music/...[/font] path from any other OpenMW data directory.

S3maphore searches OpenMW's virtual file system, so your music does not need to live inside the S3maphore archive. This is also how playlist-only modules use tracks supplied by other mods.

Some playlists register an explicit track list instead of reading an entire folder.

If a playlist cannot be toggled in the settings menu, S3maphore did not discover any of its registered tracks.

[size=4][b]Controls[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]F8[/b] — skip the current track.[/*]
[*][b]Shift+F8[/b] — toggle S3maphore music on or off.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

The S3maphore settings menu lets you:

[list]
[*]Enable debug messages.[/*]
[*]Show track and playlist names.[/*]
[*]Enable or disable combat music.[/*]
[*]Control silence tracks.[/*]
[*]Choose whether a new playlist interrupts or finishes the current track.[/*]
[*]Permanently enable or disable individual registered playlists.[/*]
[/list]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]COMPATIBILITY[/color][/center]
[/heading]

Music mods that add or replace tracks in [font=Courier New]Music/Explore[/font], [font=Courier New]Music/Battle[/font], or [font=Courier New]Music/Special[/font] work with S3maphore automatically.

Playlist-based music packs are different. Their tracks may live in custom folders, so S3maphore needs matching playlist definitions.

The included compatibility modules provide those definitions for supported MUSE-style packs, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53568]Dynamic Music[/url] soundbanks, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51734]Morrow Winds[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51769]CaptainCreepy Music Pack[/url], and other music mods.

[color=#d4d4d8][b]Important:[/b] support for another mod's music does not mean you should also run its original music-management scripts. S3maphore is the music controller.[/color]

Some mods use MWScript to play music directly. S3maphore does not change that interface.

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]TROUBLESHOOTING[/color][/center]
[/heading]

[size=4][b]No music plays at all[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]1.[/b] Confirm that [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] is enabled.[/*]
[*][b]2.[/b] Confirm that [font=Courier New]S3maphore.esp[/font] is enabled in OpenMW's content list.[/*]
[*][b]3.[/b] Confirm that H3lp Yours3lf is installed.[/*]
[*][b]4.[/b] Confirm that S3maphore's numbered directories were not flattened into [font=Courier New]Data Files[/font].[/*]
[/list]

If vanilla Explore and Battle music works, [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] is installed correctly.

[size=4][b]Vanilla music works, but an optional playlist does not[/b][/size]

Confirm that:

[list]
[*]The matching S3maphore module is enabled.[/*]
[*]The music pack it expects is installed.[/*]
[*]The expected tracks exist somewhere in OpenMW's virtual file system.[/*]
[/list]

If S3maphore finds no registered tracks for a playlist, that playlist stays inactive.

[size=4][b]Still nothing? Time to interrogate the log.[/b][/size]

Enable S3maphore debug messages and inspect [font=Courier New]openmw.log[/font].

S3maphore messages begin with:

[code][ S3MAPHORE ][/code]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]FOR PLAYLIST AUTHORS[/color][/center]
[/heading]

S3maphore playlists are Lua modules.

Use built-in rules or combine them into entirely new conditions. The public documentation covers playlist creation, priorities, rules, events, metadata, and the S3maphore interface.

[center][url=https://dreamweave-mp.github.io/S3ctors-S3cret-St4sh/s3maphore/docs/][b]Read the S3maphore playlist-author documentation[/b][/url][/center]

